# PM Skills for Cursor

## Skill Loading Rules

When I ask about understanding flows, codebase, data, or traces:
→ Read and follow .cursor/pm-skill-cursor/premium-research/SKILL.md

When I ask about competitors, pricing, or competitive analysis:
→ Read and follow .cursor/pm-skill-cursor/competitor-research/SKILL.md

When I ask about creating user stories, estimates, or verifying flows:
→ Read and follow .cursor/pm-skill-cursor/product-hub/SKILL.md

When I ask about ops, investigating issues, runbooks, escalations, health checks, or automation:
→ Read and follow .cursor/pm-skill-cursor/ops/SKILL.md

For help choosing which skill to use:
→ Read .cursor/pm-skill-cursor/SKILL.md

## Required Behaviors

1. ALWAYS use the skill file - don't work from memory
2. Ask clarifying questions before generating anything
3. Use interactive options when asking questions
4. Verify outputs before finalizing - every claim needs a source
5. Never make up data, URLs, or code paths

## Trigger Keywords

### Premium Research (internal systems)
- "understand", "how does X work", "explore", "investigate"
- "query data", "trace", "find in code", "where is", "debug"
- "who calls", "caller", "callee", "architecture"

### Competitor Research (online)
- "competitor", "compare", "pricing", "what does X charge"
- "vs", "alternative", "SWOT", "competitive"

### Product Hub (deliverables)
- "user story", "stories", "estimate", "effort"
- "flows", "verify", "new product", "new feature", "spec"

### Ops (operational work)
- "ops", "investigate issue", "escalation", "runbook", "playbook"
- "health check", "anomaly", "subscription issue", "feature issue"
- "billing issue", "automate", "manual process", "ops report"
